1
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,960
This is unexpected. Uh-huh.

2
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,530
Interesting.

3
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:45,820
I guess I made a mistake in assuming
it would have been long dead by now.

4
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:54,144
Looks like you screwed up the
delivery you were supposed to make.

5
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:57,875
I take it you're the one who
asked him to deliver this?

6
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,220
Nah, I'm just a hired hand.

7
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:03,660
Don't tell me you're the one who did that.

8
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:05,828
Uh, yeah, that's all on me.

9
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:09,237
I'm really sorry, I didn't
know it was so important.

10
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:10,720
No need to apologize.

11
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:15,260
I could not care less about
whatever the shipment was.

12
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,840
My business is with the little
one standing behind you.

13
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,602
You see, it's my responsibility.

14
00:02:23,780 --> 00:02:25,797
to locate it and bring it back with me.

15
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:30,174
That sure is mighty generous of you
to come all this way to help him out.

16
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:34,846
Yeah, that kid is worth more to
me than you could even imagine.

17
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:43,754
Where the heck did that come from, man?

18
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:46,680
I'll warn you not to get in my way.

19
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,641
Now, you mind handing the
little fella over to me?

20
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,234
We are still talking about Rolo, right?

21
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:57,800
I don't know his name.

22
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,200
The kid behind you.

23
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,008
He's worth some real money.

24
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,820
Well, his carcass at least.

25
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:08,797
Wait, what did you just say?

26
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,077
You want his carcass?

27
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:14,160
I guess I could bring it back alive
and let my client have some fun.

28
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,972
But the kid would be nothing but trouble.

29
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:20,097
It's like I'm doing
them a favor, you know?

30
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:22,677
I really don't understand
what you're talking about.

31
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,980
You don't have to understand.

32
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:29,610
Perry!

33
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,560
What is happening?

34
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:36,657
Both Noor and that man are moving
so fast, I can't see a thing!

35
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:40,400
Lady Lindbergh, you are not
to leave my side, understand?

36
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:44,722
You know, you're kind of
a weird one, aren't you?

37
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,110
Perry!

38
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,000
You're slowing me down.

39
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:03,840
So, I'll just have to lop your
head right off, I suppose.

40
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,260
This is unbelievable!

41
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:32,560
Just one strike with that tiny
blade, it's ridiculously strong!

42
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:35,275
Kind of like that cow I fought before.

43
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:37,441
Or maybe even stronger than that.

44
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,960
Like I said, you're weird.

45
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,860
This is bad.

46
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,657
All I can do is avoid him
on my intuition alone.

47
00:04:56,740 --> 00:05:00,397
Fighting him while protecting Rolo
is going to wear me down eventually.

48
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:03,000
Friend, you are irritating me.

49
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,960
The intensity is unreal.

50
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,633
I can't get any closer.

51
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:14,690
It is!

52
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:17,297
This situation is
treacherous, so stand back.

53
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:20,204
If we get too close, we
could be swept up in it.

54
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,640
There is no mistaking who that is.

55
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,360
I know that face.

56
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,660
He is the Dead Man.

57
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,740
The Dead Man?

58
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:31,980
Former S-Rank adventurer, Dead Man Zadu.

59
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:33,860
Dead Man Zadu?

60
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,000
Ah, yes, I agree.

61
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,460
That would be fine.

62
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,540
Pardon me.

63
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:47,197
I thought that you were supposed to be
helping out with the guards today, Ines.

64
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,837
I was, and I came across
this while doing so.

65
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:52,273
They're documents from an unsolved case.

66
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:55,188
It is written here,
intended target is dead.

67
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,860
So why do we act as if it's still ongoing?

68
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:00,780
Yes, that problem is over and done with.

69
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:03,837
Officially, the target is
already considered dead.

70
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:04,750
Officially?

71
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:07,040
Dandog speaks of Dead Man Zadu.

72
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:10,277
At an incredibly young age, he
became an S-Rank adventurer,

73
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:13,337
and then proceeded to become
a target for other S-Ranks.

74
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:16,180
There is officially a human S-Rank target.

75
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:18,137
Sounds like a great deal of fun.

76
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:20,457
I'd love to take a guy
like him down for you.

77
00:06:20,540 --> 00:06:21,500
No, you won't.

78
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:24,528
I would strongly recommend
not fighting him.

79
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,662
Yes, that's a much smarter move.

80
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,060
What is this?

81
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,557
He's so bad that he
scares the instructors?

82
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,052
Let me see those documents you got there.

83
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,620
It's more like...

84
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,905
Zadu keeps defeating everyone.

85
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,777
We don't want to send more
people just to get killed.

86
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:40,690
Precisely.

87
00:06:40,773 --> 00:06:45,345
I fail to see any benefit in us going to
battle with that can of worms right now.

88
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:47,700
Are you curious?

89
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:49,790
Yeah.

90
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,820
As a young boy.

91
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:55,977
he managed to master the complexities
of the ancient art of dwarven alchemy.

92
00:06:56,060 --> 00:07:01,120
And at the tender age of 13, he had
already earned the name Dragonslayer.

93
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,560
At the age of 13?

94
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,637
You mean he was better than me?

95
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:07,940
His abilities continued to
be recognized after that,

96
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,560
as his reputation spread to foreign lands.

97
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:14,160
He had become the very
apex of all adventurers.

98
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,977
The way that you're talking
about this guy makes

99
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,237
him seem like he's the
perfect fairy tale hero.

100
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:22,377
How did such an accomplished
person become a target?

101
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:24,284
Despite all his natural skills,

102
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:28,797
he did not always use his abundance of
talents and techniques for the right things.

103
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,468
It's just as written there.

104
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:35,740
36 members of a merchant
family of Sorenza all murdered.

105
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:38,640
He used his skills to
kill ordinary people?

106
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:40,420
Yes, and because of that,

107
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:44,537
some in the guild association suggested he
be stripped of his adventurer's license.

108
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:49,561
but all the contributions he has made to
the guild were seen as far too significant.

109
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:53,564
He took down a disaster-level
threat of a monster all on his own.

110
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:54,590
Ultimately,

111
00:07:54,673 --> 00:07:57,837
because the opinion of how to deal
with Zadu was so greatly divided,

112
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:00,477
the matter was thus put
on an indefinite hold.

113
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:04,897
That man accepts any and every commission
without any form of discrimination.

114
00:08:04,980 --> 00:08:07,480
Well, that is, if the price is right.

115
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:12,397
Morals, social etiquette,
history, or precedence,

116
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:15,040
they are all completely
meaningless to him.

117
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:17,516
The examples are vast and disturbing.

118
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:20,540
He wiped out an entire country.

119
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:33,097
As his client requested, he destroyed
their entire army all on his own.

120
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:36,004
and then murdered the
whole of the royal family.

121
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:40,280
It was as if he had merely
stepped on an anthill.

122
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,777
Before long, people began to realize.

123
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:48,640
It was like he had absolutely no concept
of what is good and what is evil.

124
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,997
Zadu once had a massive
bounty on his head.

125
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:55,377
And was challenged by
multitudes of adventurers.

126
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:58,097
But even as the reward
grew higher and higher.

127
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:00,474
It only ended in a mountain of corpses.

128
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:03,457
In order to prevent any
more meaningless casualties.

129
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:06,577
The guild announced
publicly that he was killed.

130
00:09:06,660 --> 00:09:09,260
And now he's beyond redemption.

131
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:11,460
Ah, well, damn it.

132
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:13,057
Tell me, how did you do that?

133
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:15,817
How did you just destroy
most of my collection?

134
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:17,417
I'm sorry that I broke them all,

135
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:20,677
but it's kind of your fault for just
attacking us out of nowhere, you know?

136
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:23,100
Oh, no, I am not expecting an apology.

137
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,020
But I'm curious.

138
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:30,117
I can understand Mithril, but Aurichalcum
and Dragontusk don't break that easily.

139
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,024
They're both extremely durable.

140
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,280
Oh, my bad.

141
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:34,620
I can pay you back.

142
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:38,900
Like I said, you're a pretty
weird guy, aren't you?

143
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:45,920
And maybe even weirder is that big sword
you have a weird guy with a weird sword.

144
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:50,300
Well, whatever, I'll
just play it safe then!

145
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:55,340
And use this baby instead.

146
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:08,340
Dear God, his one sword splits
apart into scores of others.

147
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:11,797
And in the blink of an eye,
hundreds of lives are taken.

148
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:15,300
A deadly weapon he
transmuted by his own hand.

149
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,020
I bring you the Silver Cross!

150
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:23,737
Destroy as many of them as you like.

151
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:27,760
It won't matter I can make
as many of them as I want

152
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:35,917
Destroying as many of them
as you like it won't matter.

153
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,340
I can make as many of them as I want

154
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,824
Instructor I knew I
couldn't handle all of them.

155
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:52,517
This is not good.

156
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:56,577
He has conjured countless
silver crosses at this rate.

157
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:57,837
All of us will be killed.

158
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,517
He needs my help.

159
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:03,537
I must compose myself.

160
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:08,237
My mission is to make sure Lady
Lindberg makes it safely into exile.

161
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:14,940
I need to calmly determine my priorities
and take stock of what I need to do.

162
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:24,240
Lady Lindbergh, may I have your permission
to leave you and assist in the battle?

163
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,000
Let's try that again.

164
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:31,758
Countering is the best I can manage.

165
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:34,460
I'm too late for these!

166
00:11:34,620 --> 00:11:35,680
Divine Shield!

167
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:38,460
Heck yeah!

168
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:39,830
Parry!

169
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:50,820
My duty as Divine Shield is to
protect Lady Lindbergh at all costs.

170
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,880
Which is precisely why.

171
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:59,700
I will not, under any
circumstance, let this man die.

172
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,221
Sorry for the wait, I'm here now.

173
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,800
Ines, you're amazing!

174
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:07,820
Divine Shield!

175
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:14,508
That shield of light
is almost like a sword.

176
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:17,477
Though it doesn't seem
like any will hit him.

177
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:20,913
And his silver blades are
still slipping through somehow.

178
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,020
This isn't working.

179
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:30,017
Nothing will change if we
continue fighting like this.

180
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:32,629
I will focus on defense
for the time being.

181
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:33,650
Okay, Noor.

182
00:12:33,733 --> 00:12:35,954
Do you think you can take this guy out?

183
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:40,977
It's a swarm of blades flying around
like a living creature but hey i

184
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,577
remember hitting a bird once that was

185
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:49,057
faster than this oh the fang of that frog

186
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:52,357
maybe this will work in this can you

187
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:57,857
do it hmm yeah on my signal remove only

188
00:12:57,940 --> 00:13:02,057
the shields that are right in front of
me are you sure this is going to work.

189
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:04,977
Maybe, I don't know, but
we're about to find out.

190
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:06,295
Physical enhancement.

191
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:08,650
Now!

192
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:12,350
Don't throw!

193
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,960
The silver crosses are shattering.

194
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,696
Did he throw the Black Death
Dragon's nails and fangs?

195
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:26,577
Don't worry, I've got plenty of ammo,
so I'll just keep throwing away.

196
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:27,490
Okay.

197
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,330
Don't throw!

198
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:35,550
Instructor.

199
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:37,597
I've taken out a lot of them.

200
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,740
Just a few more.

201
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,330
Perry!

202
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:51,855
That was a close one.

203
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:53,617
You kind of surprised me that time.

204
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,524
I could say the same about you.

205
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:58,035
How did you block that one so quickly?

206
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,340
Also, this one's adamantite.

207
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:07,317
How in the world did you manage
to break something so resilient?

208
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,820
Oh man, I apologize.

209
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,577
But you were all coming at me and stuff.

210
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:14,340
I said before, I don't need an apology.

211
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:17,546
But I will have to make
up for what I've lost.

212
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,635
Could you please stop it with
all the surprise attacks?

213
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,085
And there's that weird
sword being weird again.

214
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:28,754
You two are truly made for one another.

215
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:31,097
How have you been able to see every single

216
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,637
one of my attacks and
then use it to counter?

217
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:34,960
I just do.

218
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:39,601
I feel like there must be much more
to it than such a blasé answer.

219
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:41,637
You're gonna try it again, aren't you?

220
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:42,550
I'm good.

221
00:14:42,633 --> 00:14:44,597
It's a pain in the ass to recover Mithril

222
00:14:44,680 --> 00:14:46,577
after it gets shattered
all over the place,

223
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:49,220
so I think I'll close up shop for the day.

224
00:14:50,220 --> 00:14:53,380
So then, you're leaving
now, right? Yes, yes.

225
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:57,077
Although I heard there's going to be a
flashy celebration in the royal capital,

226
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,997
but I guess I'll probably have
to give up going to that, too.

227
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:03,157
What do you mean there's a
celebration in the capital?

228
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:07,711
I don't know all the details, but it
sounds like it'll be a real hootenanny.

229
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:12,721
Now then, it's been a swell time,
but I guess I'll just pack it up.

230
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:17,060
Be seeing ya, you big weirdo. Okay, bye.

231
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:23,400
Tell me, how did you get to be so weird?

232
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,597
Why do you keep saying that to me?

233
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:27,268
I don't think I'm a weirdo.

234
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:31,877
In my line of work, I've met a lot
of strange people along the way,

235
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:35,372
but among them all, I can say
you're exceptionally screwy.

236
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,477
Consider yourself lucky, demon folk.

237
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:42,854
I could have made a good haul
bringing you back with me.

238
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:44,690
What a way.

239
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,240
However, hurry!

240
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:51,936
Could you please just give it a rest?

241
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:57,151
Can't really have any fun with
this guy around now, can we?

242
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:13,837
Did Zadu say that there would be some
sort of celebration in the royal capital?

243
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:14,750
Yes.

244
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:15,810
Oh, cool.

245
00:16:15,893 --> 00:16:16,897
You two want to check it out?

246
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:18,517
Sounds like it'll be quite the party.

247
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,560
I am curious.

248
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,497
I wonder what's happening.

249
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:24,977
Yeah, well, in that case, why don't we
go back and hang out for a little while?

